# Independent errors in two statements are both reported: an unknown column and a type error.
mode: check
schema: 'orders.csv'(orderId: string, customerId: string, amount: real, qty: long, small: int, timestamp: datetime, wait: timespan, shipped: bool)
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | where amout > 1;
from 'orders.csv' | where orderId > 1
---- expected
error[DS1001]: unknown column `amout`
  --> query:1:27
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | where amout > 1;
  |                           ^^^^^ no column named `amout` here
  |
  = help: a column with a similar name exists: `amount`
  = note: columns available at this point: orderId, customerId, amount, qty, small, timestamp, wait, shipped

error[DS2003]: cannot compare `string` with `long`
  --> query:2:27
  |
2 | from 'orders.csv' | where orderId > 1
  |                           ^^^^^^^   - this is `long`
  |                           |
  |                           this is `string` (column `orderId` was read from orders.csv)
  |
  = help: if `orderId` holds `long` values, convert it first: `tolong(orderId) > 1`
